1
00:00:11,635 --> 00:00:13,470
[BIRD SQUAWKING]

2
00:00:31,863 --> 00:00:33,948
[DOG WHINES]

3
00:00:35,575 --> 00:00:38,244
Hmm? [CHUCKLES]

4
00:00:44,751 --> 00:00:47,212
All right, Radar. Okay, come on. Let's go.

5
00:00:56,347 --> 00:00:59,433
[TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWS]

6
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:19,745
[SIGHS]

7
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:28,671
[SMACKS LIPS]

8
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:46,314
Hmm?

9
00:01:56,073 --> 00:01:57,158
[SIGHS]

10
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:30,484
["ACE OF SPADES" PLAYING]

11
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:09,898
[GRUNTS]

12
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:20,075
[MUSIC STOPS]

13
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,784
[WHIRRING]

14
00:04:45,578 --> 00:04:49,666
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGING]

15
00:04:55,755 --> 00:04:57,298
[WHIRRING STOPS]

16
00:05:25,201 --> 00:05:26,702
-Going good?
-Yep.

17
00:05:26,786 --> 00:05:27,870
Yeah?

18
00:05:29,747 --> 00:05:31,897
-Think you'll have it by…
-I'll get there.

19
00:05:32,334 --> 00:05:34,211
[HELLY TYPING]

20
00:05:54,231 --> 00:05:57,234
-She's not gonna make it, is she?
-Uh, you should be at your desks.

21
00:05:57,318 --> 00:05:59,778
We've both been done a week.
What is there to do?

22
00:05:59,862 --> 00:06:01,821
-Is she gonna make it?
-She's gonna make it.

23
00:06:01,905 --> 00:06:02,906
Mark.

24
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:03,990
Yes?

25
00:06:04,074 --> 00:06:06,327
-IRVING: Don't laugh.
-At?

26
00:06:07,036 --> 00:06:10,372
I just wonder if it might be
helpful for us to stand behind her

27
00:06:10,456 --> 00:06:12,458
and perhaps chant her name.

28
00:06:15,377 --> 00:06:18,839
Okay. She'll make it. Just let her focus.

29
00:06:24,803 --> 00:06:26,180
[HELLY TYPING SLOWLY]

30
00:06:28,974 --> 00:06:30,142
How's she doing?

31
00:06:30,684 --> 00:06:32,684
MR. MILCHICK: Gonna be down to the wire.

32
00:06:39,026 --> 00:06:40,326
MS. COBEL: She'll make it.

33
00:06:41,028 --> 00:06:43,197
Let's prep for when she makes it.

34
00:06:48,118 --> 00:06:49,744
Oh. And I want to schedule

35
00:06:49,828 --> 00:06:52,873
a end-of-the-quarter
wellness session for Mark…

36
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:55,501
One last time.

37
00:06:58,045 --> 00:06:59,171
Really?

38
00:07:04,636 --> 00:07:05,637
Seth.

39
00:07:07,013 --> 00:07:09,682
I know that this has
been a trying quarter,

40
00:07:09,766 --> 00:07:11,935
and you have availed yourself well.

41
00:07:14,229 --> 00:07:16,982
Mr. Graner sits with Kier now,

42
00:07:17,774 --> 00:07:20,902
and I imagine they're
both very satisfied with you.

43
00:07:37,085 --> 00:07:38,086
[SIGHS]

44
00:07:40,922 --> 00:07:42,507
[TYPING CONTINUES]

45
00:07:52,517 --> 00:07:53,893
HELLY: Hey.

46
00:07:55,812 --> 00:07:56,813
Did you…

47
00:07:57,439 --> 00:07:58,523
I think I did.

48
00:08:04,237 --> 00:08:06,323
[TRIUMPHANT MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:15,080
-She do it?
-MARK: She did it!

50
00:08:17,917 --> 00:08:19,168
Fuck and yes.

51
00:08:19,252 --> 00:08:22,505
-Oh, my goodness.
-[ALL CHUCKLE]

52
00:08:41,274 --> 00:08:43,944
<i>I knew you could do it, Helly R.</i>

53
00:08:44,028 --> 00:08:45,362
MARK: Oh. [CHUCKLES]

54
00:08:45,446 --> 00:08:48,574
<i>Even in your darkest moments,
I could see you arriving here.</i>

55
00:08:50,284 --> 00:08:54,830
<i>In refining your macrodata file, you have
brought glory to this company and to me.</i>

56
00:08:55,623 --> 00:08:56,957
<i>Kier Eagan.</i>

57
00:08:57,458 --> 00:09:00,711
<i>I… I love you.</i>

58
00:09:01,837 --> 00:09:05,424
<i>But now I must away, for there are
others who need me around the world.</i>

59
00:09:06,342 --> 00:09:09,679
<i>Goodbye, Helly R., and thank you.</i>

60
00:09:24,276 --> 00:09:26,612
-[MUSIC ENDS]
-[SIGHS DEEPLY]

61
00:09:26,696 --> 00:09:30,074
Boom! That's quota. We did it.

62
00:09:30,783 --> 00:09:31,784
Good work.

63
00:09:36,372 --> 00:09:37,456
So it's on now?

64
00:09:39,709 --> 00:09:41,752
BOTH LAUGHING:

65
00:09:44,422 --> 00:09:45,548
-Oh!
-Oh.

66
00:09:53,973 --> 00:09:56,808
Oh, Mark. I don't know how you knew

67
00:09:56,892 --> 00:09:59,854
for the end of the quarter
I wanted a heart attack.

68
00:10:02,356 --> 00:10:05,943
Well, uh, we made it,
despite a staffing shake-up.

69
00:10:06,027 --> 00:10:10,197
[CHUCKLES] Yes, and spending half
of your time farting around the halls.

70
00:10:10,281 --> 00:10:12,909
Still, yes. You made it.

71
00:10:12,993 --> 00:10:16,455
Have you decided who you
want to stay for the waffle party?

72
00:10:16,997 --> 00:10:18,206
I was thinking Dylan.

73
00:10:21,710 --> 00:10:25,213
You know you can choose
yourself or anyone but Dylan.

74
00:10:26,048 --> 00:10:31,053
Yeah… [STAMMERS] …but it's more
his thing, and he really worked hard.

75
00:10:31,595 --> 00:10:32,596
MS. COBEL: Hmm.

76
00:10:34,264 --> 00:10:36,599
[BOTH CHUCKLE]

77
00:10:36,683 --> 00:10:38,685
Oh. Well, I'll make the arrangements.

78
00:10:39,269 --> 00:10:40,919
-Great.
-But before you celebrate,

79
00:10:41,688 --> 00:10:43,523
I'd like you to drop by wellness.

80
00:10:43,607 --> 00:10:44,607
Really?

81
00:10:44,691 --> 00:10:48,320
Yes. I'm having all department
heads do it end-of-quarter.

82
00:10:49,154 --> 00:10:53,659
With all of this stress and
Mr. Graner retiring and everything.

83
00:10:55,035 --> 00:10:56,036
Of course.

84
00:10:56,620 --> 00:10:58,205
[BOTH LAUGH]

85
00:11:01,249 --> 00:11:03,377
Mark, all sarcasm aside…

86
00:11:04,294 --> 00:11:05,504
Yeah.

87
00:11:07,172 --> 00:11:08,215
Thank you.

88
00:11:09,257 --> 00:11:11,218
Uh, I…

89
00:11:12,052 --> 00:11:13,929
Lumon needed this.

90
00:11:22,396 --> 00:11:23,480
[DOOR OPENS]

91
00:11:26,942 --> 00:11:27,943
Mark.

92
00:11:29,111 --> 00:11:30,195
Ms. Casey.

93
00:11:38,704 --> 00:11:39,871
Where'd the tree go?

94
00:11:43,166 --> 00:11:44,376
You can have a seat.

95
00:11:49,090 --> 00:11:50,591
Why's everything in boxes?

96
00:11:52,635 --> 00:11:56,681
[SIGHS] Evidently Lumon's been
blessed with a new wellness director.

97
00:11:58,057 --> 00:12:01,101
So I'll be retiring at the conclusion
of this session, and the room is…

98
00:12:01,185 --> 00:12:02,353
What? Wait.

99
00:12:03,438 --> 00:12:04,689
When did they tell you?

100
00:12:07,942 --> 00:12:10,653
Just now. Just a moment ago.

101
00:12:17,285 --> 00:12:19,620
[SOOTHING MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:12:30,923 --> 00:12:31,966
Mark S.,

103
00:12:33,176 --> 00:12:37,096
you have successfully led your
department, Macrodata Refinement,

104
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:38,848
to meet their quarterly quota,

105
00:12:39,641 --> 00:12:44,061
and are thus eligible for this
special, augmented wellness session.

106
00:12:44,145 --> 00:12:45,980
I didn't think you'd get fired.

107
00:12:49,567 --> 00:12:51,903
"Your outie is kind.

108
00:12:53,071 --> 00:12:58,326
"Your outie has brightened
people's days by merely smiling."

109
00:12:59,243 --> 00:13:02,871
Your outie makes time
for people, even when…"

110
00:13:02,955 --> 00:13:04,624
Hey, let me talk to somebody.

111
00:13:07,794 --> 00:13:08,878
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

112
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:19,472
I really liked being in the
office with you all that day.

113
00:13:22,476 --> 00:13:23,978
I know I vexed you.

114
00:13:24,645 --> 00:13:27,272
I know I'm… strange.

115
00:13:28,065 --> 00:13:30,401
No, you're not strange.

116
00:13:31,110 --> 00:13:33,737
My life has been 107 hours long.

117
00:13:34,571 --> 00:13:37,366
Most of that has been
these half-hour sessions.

118
00:13:39,451 --> 00:13:43,538
For me, my favorite
time was the eight hours

119
00:13:43,622 --> 00:13:47,459
I spent in your department watching Helly.

120
00:13:50,254 --> 00:13:52,589
It's the longest I've ever been awake.

121
00:13:56,427 --> 00:13:59,221
I suppose it's what you
could call my good old days.

122
00:14:04,435 --> 00:14:06,186
There must be something we can do.

123
00:14:16,113 --> 00:14:18,407
Why do you care what happens to me?

124
00:14:31,503 --> 00:14:34,882
<i>Because we're people, not parts of people.</i>

125
00:14:36,091 --> 00:14:39,178
<i>Even with what little they
gave us, these are our lives.</i>

126
00:14:41,013 --> 00:14:43,098
<i>No one gets to just turn you off.</i>

127
00:14:48,687 --> 00:14:50,022
You're nice, Mark.

128
00:14:57,572 --> 00:14:58,573
[CHUCKLES]

129
00:15:07,332 --> 00:15:09,709
"Your outie is kind.

130
00:15:11,294 --> 00:15:16,174
"Your outie can set up a
tent in under three minutes."

131
00:15:17,717 --> 00:15:22,097
"Your outie knows a
beautiful rock from a plain one."

132
00:15:23,515 --> 00:15:25,808
<i>Your outie likes giving…"</i>

133
00:15:25,892 --> 00:15:27,018
[PLAYBACK STOPS]

134
00:15:27,102 --> 00:15:29,102
MR. MILCHICK: You know it's good, right?

135
00:15:30,230 --> 00:15:32,030
That they don't remember each other?

136
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,194
It means the chips work.

137
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:39,906
It's a win.

138
00:15:43,827 --> 00:15:45,495
Take her back down

139
00:15:47,038 --> 00:15:49,582
to the testing floor, please.

140
00:15:58,383 --> 00:15:59,509
[DOOR CLOSES]

141
00:16:31,375 --> 00:16:33,127
[BREATHES SHAKILY]

142
00:16:41,302 --> 00:16:43,304
[MS. CASEY SIGHS]

143
00:16:45,473 --> 00:16:48,643
Do you know if I'm happy up there?

144
00:16:50,269 --> 00:16:51,270
Of course.

145
00:16:52,146 --> 00:16:54,607
You do all sorts of wonderful things.

146
00:17:12,708 --> 00:17:14,376
-Could I just…
-I'm sorry.

147
00:17:15,461 --> 00:17:17,061
I just have so much to do today.

148
00:17:17,797 --> 00:17:19,131
On you go.

149
00:17:43,864 --> 00:17:44,914
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

150
00:17:58,838 --> 00:18:00,589
-Mark.
-Where were you?

151
00:18:00,673 --> 00:18:02,550
They gave me a wellness check.

152
00:18:03,342 --> 00:18:06,013
Okay. You're all set for the waffle party.

153
00:18:06,638 --> 00:18:07,639
How's Ms. Casey?

154
00:18:07,723 --> 00:18:10,223
I mean, I'm over her,
but I still wanna be friends.

155
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:14,562
-They fired her.
-What?

156
00:18:14,646 --> 00:18:15,730
MARK: Yeah. She just found out.

157
00:18:15,814 --> 00:18:18,314
Well, can we help her?
Is there anything we can do?

158
00:18:19,026 --> 00:18:20,152
I don't know.

159
00:18:22,195 --> 00:18:24,114
Is everyone sure they wanna do this?

160
00:18:25,157 --> 00:18:27,659
MR. MILCHICK: Any
Macrodats ready to party?

161
00:18:29,077 --> 00:18:30,078
Yeah.

162
00:18:33,540 --> 00:18:36,190
Dylan G.'s waffle party will
commence at close of day.

163
00:18:36,752 --> 00:18:38,127
In the meantime,

164
00:18:38,211 --> 00:18:41,965
I've ordered the pre-waffle
party egg bar social for everyone.

165
00:18:42,799 --> 00:18:45,927
Yes! Pay dirt! Yeah!

166
00:18:46,011 --> 00:18:49,014
All of you deserve
this for reaching quota.

167
00:18:49,681 --> 00:18:51,308
But before we begin…

168
00:18:53,435 --> 00:18:57,689
A very special gift for
a very special Dylan.

169
00:18:58,565 --> 00:19:01,360
Our three-time R of the Q!

170
00:19:02,110 --> 00:19:04,988
A man whose mind is
as sharp as his incisors.

171
00:19:05,530 --> 00:19:06,573
Right, bud?

172
00:19:07,949 --> 00:19:09,785
[CHUCKLES]

173
00:19:14,831 --> 00:19:15,873
Open it.

174
00:19:15,957 --> 00:19:19,627
Yeah, I bet you'd like that, fuckers.
But, uh, my prize, my eyes, so…

175
00:19:19,711 --> 00:19:21,463
Maybe you should show them, Dylan.

176
00:19:21,963 --> 00:19:23,674
Show them what you requested.

177
00:19:25,092 --> 00:19:26,385
Yeah, show us, man.

178
00:19:27,302 --> 00:19:28,470
Fine. Um…

179
00:19:41,776 --> 00:19:44,028
Okay, yeah.
Let's switch up the vibe in here.

180
00:19:50,493 --> 00:19:51,493
Good?

181
00:19:51,577 --> 00:19:54,205
[FUNKY MUSIC PLAYING]

182
00:20:13,850 --> 00:20:16,519
Jesus, this is actually good.

183
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:19,314
Yeah, the egg bar is coveted as fuck.

184
00:20:27,530 --> 00:20:29,448
Look at this thing over here.

185
00:20:29,532 --> 00:20:30,742
Looking good.

186
00:20:34,537 --> 00:20:35,538
[SHUTTER CLICKS]

187
00:20:39,250 --> 00:20:41,085
I should be the one to stay behind.

188
00:20:41,919 --> 00:20:42,962
Nope.

189
00:20:44,964 --> 00:20:46,714
Don't you wanna see your kid again?

190
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:50,150
What we're doing
tonight is just the first step.

191
00:20:54,307 --> 00:20:55,475
Are you sure?

192
00:21:23,921 --> 00:21:26,298
Helly R.
attempted suicide three weeks ago.

193
00:21:28,634 --> 00:21:29,802
Yes, she did.

194
00:21:32,513 --> 00:21:33,813
How could you not tell us?

195
00:21:36,183 --> 00:21:37,893
Did Milchick give you those?

196
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:41,355
Answer the question.

197
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:45,067
Am I speaking with the Board?

198
00:21:47,403 --> 00:21:49,446
We also know that
you've been spending time

199
00:21:49,530 --> 00:21:51,490
at the home of Mark Scout's sister.

200
00:21:55,202 --> 00:21:56,203
Right.

201
00:21:57,204 --> 00:22:01,959
It has been decided that you be suspended
from your position, effective immediately.

202
00:22:03,836 --> 00:22:04,962
You are fired.

203
00:22:07,047 --> 00:22:08,298
Go f…

204
00:22:09,216 --> 00:22:10,259
[SCOFFS]

205
00:22:10,968 --> 00:22:13,012
Oh, fuck off, Natalie!

206
00:22:14,221 --> 00:22:16,181
[SCOFFS] Is the Board even there?

207
00:22:22,354 --> 00:22:23,647
BOARD MEMBER: <i>Yes.</i>

208
00:22:33,073 --> 00:22:35,492
[SIGHS] I'm sorry. That was rude.

209
00:22:36,952 --> 00:22:40,706
I can explain everything
to the Board tonight, please.

210
00:22:44,460 --> 00:22:46,110
The Board has concluded the call.

211
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:25,167
"Endow in each swing of your ax

212
00:23:25,251 --> 00:23:29,381
"or swipe of your pen the
sum of your affections,"

213
00:23:30,256 --> 00:23:33,343
"that through me they may be purified"

214
00:23:34,427 --> 00:23:35,762
"and returned."

215
00:23:39,599 --> 00:23:42,185
"No higher purpose
may be found than this."

216
00:23:44,854 --> 00:23:48,692
Nor any… higher love."

217
00:24:16,344 --> 00:24:18,179
[LAUGHS]

218
00:24:18,263 --> 00:24:19,472
I figured it out.

219
00:24:20,390 --> 00:24:22,351
The goats lay the eggs.

220
00:24:22,435 --> 00:24:23,686
Oh, my God. You got it!

221
00:24:27,356 --> 00:24:29,025
[HELLY CHUCKLES]

222
00:24:39,160 --> 00:24:40,453
You scared about tonight?

223
00:24:42,830 --> 00:24:45,499
Uh… Yeah.

224
00:24:48,836 --> 00:24:51,547
I'm scared of getting caught.

225
00:24:53,883 --> 00:24:54,884
Oh.

226
00:24:55,801 --> 00:24:58,971
They left us unattended, and
thought we'd be too dumb to notice.

227
00:25:00,014 --> 00:25:01,599
They won't see this coming.

228
00:25:05,102 --> 00:25:06,562
Or we won't wake up.

229
00:25:17,573 --> 00:25:19,200
Or we're all assholes out there.

230
00:25:20,910 --> 00:25:23,204
-Well, that's a given for me.
-[CHUCKLES]

231
00:25:26,248 --> 00:25:30,628
You know, I… I just hope it turns
out I have things I care about.

232
00:25:31,671 --> 00:25:32,797
Like, for real.

233
00:25:35,883 --> 00:25:38,010
You pretended to care
about me pretty well.

234
00:25:43,182 --> 00:25:45,685
You're…
You're easy to pretend to care about.

235
00:25:53,150 --> 00:25:54,151
Thank you.

236
00:25:56,947 --> 00:25:57,948
As are you.

237
00:25:58,448 --> 00:25:59,449
Thanks.

238
00:26:03,120 --> 00:26:04,454
Okay, Refiners!

239
00:26:05,414 --> 00:26:08,514
I need to see about a management
issue, and this party is over.

240
00:26:10,043 --> 00:26:11,544
I'll leave the food.

241
00:26:11,628 --> 00:26:13,129
Thank you, Mr. Milchick.

242
00:26:13,213 --> 00:26:16,717
Dylan, I'll be back to escort
you to perpetuity shortly.

243
00:26:53,837 --> 00:26:54,838
Key card.

244
00:26:56,256 --> 00:26:57,382
[SIGHS]

245
00:27:10,437 --> 00:27:11,605
On you go then.

246
00:27:34,629 --> 00:27:37,464
Okay, look, you don't mess
with any other departments.

247
00:27:37,548 --> 00:27:39,008
-It's just us three.
-I know.

248
00:27:39,884 --> 00:27:41,594
The machine's designed
to be operated by two…

249
00:27:41,678 --> 00:27:43,012
Two people. I'll be fine.

250
00:27:43,096 --> 00:27:44,546
Can I have the stuff, please?

251
00:27:51,604 --> 00:27:54,607
Now, look, it's likely we'll
all wake up around people.

252
00:27:54,691 --> 00:27:57,818
Could be driving or skiing,
whatever we do up there.

253
00:27:57,902 --> 00:28:00,070
So be ready for anything
as you go up the elevator.

254
00:28:00,154 --> 00:28:01,155
Okay?

255
00:28:01,739 --> 00:28:04,992
The important thing is you find
someone it seems you can trust,

256
00:28:05,076 --> 00:28:07,286
and you tell them everything.

257
00:28:07,370 --> 00:28:09,330
And we don't know how long
Dylan will be able to give us,

258
00:28:09,414 --> 00:28:11,624
so we can't get distracted
digging into our lives.

259
00:28:11,708 --> 00:28:13,751
Right. The mission is the priority.

260
